To calculate the angle of the force for a given momentum, you can use the `calculate_vector_angle` tool from our tools section. This function requires two parameters: the X and Y components of the force vector. The angle will be returned in either degrees (if set to True) or radians (if set to False).

Here's how you would call this function:

```json
{
  "name": "calculate_vector_angle",
  "arguments": {
    "X_component": 10,
    "Y_component": 5,
    "use_degrees": true
  }
}
```

This example assumes that the force vector has an X-component of 10 units and a Y-component of 5 units. The `use_degrees` parameter is set to `true`, so the output will be in degrees. If you want the angle in radians instead, simply change the value of `use_degrees` to `false`.
